      "original_record": {
        "id": "R04",
        "prompt": "Use case: historical-scene. R04 documentary illustration. One wide 16:9 painterly oil painting, visibly painted rather than photographic. A modest ancient Greek household storeroom with several huge terracotta storage pithoi half buried in the earthen floor. Broad round bellies partly below ground, wide open-mouthed shapes but every mouth covered by a simple closed terracotta lid; raised horizontal bands and small sturdy lug handles. Doorway daylight softly crosses the dusty floor. Large utilitarian storage vessels, not small amphorae, flowerpots, boxes or coffins. Quiet atmosphere, stable architectural perspective. No people, hands, faces, bodies, human figures on pottery, statues, nudity, text, inscriptions, watermark or captions. Generic artistic reconstruction, no exact famous archaeological site.",
